       <h1>Abdul El-Sayed Wins Michigan Senate Race to Become US's First Muslim Senator</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Democrat Abdul El-Sayed defeated Republican Mike Rogers in Michigan's crucial US Senate race during the 2026 midterm elections, making history as the country's first Muslim senator. The high-stakes contest for the seat vacated by retiring Democratic Senator Gary Peters drew intense focus as both parties battled for control of the upper chamber. El-Sayed campaigned on a progressive platform centred on universal healthcare and a populist economic message. His victory provides a vital boost for Democrats seeking to maintain their majority in the state.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/abdul-el-sayed-wins-michigan-senate-race-to-become-uss-first.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the outcome of the Michigan Senate race and El-Sayed's historic win without padding.</p>
