     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-04 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>IIT Delhi Retains Top Spot, DU Exits Top 100 in QS Asia Rankings 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Rankings</span> <span>#IIT Delhi</span> <span>#DU</span></div>
       <p>New data from the QS Asia Rankings 2027, as reported by ET Education, reveals significant shifts for prominent Indian institutions. The rankings show that IIT Delhi has successfully retained its top position within the latest assessment.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/iit-delhi-retains-top-spot-du-exits-top-100-in-qs-asia-ranki.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Conversely, Delhi University (DU) has seen a notable change in its standing, exiting the top 100 in the QS Asia Rankings 2027. This marks a distinct performance difference compared to IIT Delhi's consistent placement.</p><p>What to watch: Future performance of Indian universities in upcoming rankings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports the core facts from the provided source snippet.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
