     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Iran Endorses US Voters' 'No To War' Message and Warns Washington</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Iranian Parliament Speaker Mohammad Baqer Ghalibaf has endorsed the anti-war sentiment expressed by American voters during the US midterm elections. Warning Washington against resuming military action, Ghalibaf stated that ignoring public will to serve international paymasters would bring a 'nightmare'. The remarks coincide with ongoing indirect negotiations mediated by Qatar, as Tehran demands the US waive oil sanctions, end its naval blockade, and release frozen funds. Meanwhile, US President Donald Trump has maintained that the military option remains open, stating he is ready if necessary.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/iran-endorses-us-voters-no-to-war-message-and-warns-washingt.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures Ghalibaf's endorsement of the US anti-war sentiment, his warning to Washington, and Trump's response.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/iran-ghalibaf-warns-us-no-to-war-message-donald-trump-ws-l-10412059.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
