     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-04 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Raichur District Spends ₹4,805.24 Crore Across Five Guarantee Schemes Led by Gruha Lakshmi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Karnataka’s five flagship guarantee schemes have reached every eligible beneficiary across Raichur district, with total expenditures reaching ₹4,805.24 crore up to July 2026. State Guarantee Schemes Implementation Authority Vice-President P.T. Parameshwar Naik announced the spending figures following a review meeting in Raichur on November 3.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/raichur-district-spends-480524-crore-across-five-guarantee-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The largest allocation went to the Gruha Lakshmi scheme with ₹2,744.81 crore disbursed. Remaining disbursements included ₹806.22 crore for Anna Bhagya, ₹618.03 crore for the Shakti scheme, ₹557.31 crore for Gruha Jyothi, and ₹78.87 crore for Yuva Nidhi, ensuring welfare delivery without leakages as promised by the Congress party.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately details the guarantee scheme spending figures and attribution without padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/480524-crore-spent-under-five-guarantee-schemes-in-raichur/article71661424.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
