       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Railway Track Sabotage Investigated in Rajasthan</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A powerful explosion damaged the Anupgarh-Suratgarh railway track in Rajasthan’s Sriganganagar district on Tuesday night. The blast occurred near 50 GB village, shattering two concrete sleepers, dislodging track clips, and creating a two-foot-deep crater. A passenger train had safely crossed the site just 45 minutes prior.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/railway-track-sabotage-investigated-in-rajasthan.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Authorities have launched a multi-agency investigation involving the National Investigation Agency and the Anti-Terrorism Squad. North-Western Railway canceled four train services as a precaution while forensic experts analyze explosive substances used in the blast. The district police are currently awaiting forensic reports to determine the exact nature of the incident.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures all critical details from the wire report effectively.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
