       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-11-04 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Wall Street Stock Futures Surge Following Democratic US Midterm Congressional Wins</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Wall Street stocks rallied after Democrats secured majorities in both chambers of the US Congress in the midterm elections, easing concerns over political uncertainty. Futures linked to the Dow Jones Industrial Average surged 1,083 points, or 2.1%, while S&amp;P 500 futures rose 1.1% and Nasdaq-100 futures gained 0.4%. Investors welcomed the prospect of political gridlock, believing a divided government will act as a check on presidential policies. Despite the broader market gains, artificial intelligence stocks faced pressure over potential data centre restrictions and proposed moratoriums.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/wall-street-stock-futures-surge-following-democratic-us-midt.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures market movements, political gridlock analysis, and sector reactions accurately.</p>
