       <h1>West Indies Seek Rare Series Win in Sylhet as Bangladesh Plan Changes</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Leading 1-0 after an eight-wicket victory in Dhaka, West Indies aim to secure a rare away series win against Bangladesh in Sylhet to cap off an unbeaten calendar year. Head coach Daren Sammy praised his spin attack, featuring Jomel Warrican and Roston Chase, which outbowled Bangladesh in the opener. Bangladesh are desperate for a batting recovery after squandering a strong start, despite Shadman Islam's century. In a major boost for the hosts, Mushfiqur Rahim will return to the playing XI following a finger injury that sidelined him during the first Test.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-04/west-indies-seek-rare-series-win-in-sylhet-as-bangladesh-pla.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise summary covering West Indies' series lead, Sammy's praise of the spin attack, and Mushfiqur Rahim's return.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
